    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup for May 7th is spearheaded by **Brady House** and **Nasim Nunez**, both of whom benefit significantly from a favorable matchup against Woods Richardson. **Brady House** enters as our top-rated play (63.81) due to a robust 19% boost from the opposing SP skill and a positive platoon advantage, while **Nasim Nunez** continues to provide high-leverage value (62.09). Though **Nasim Nunez** suffers a slight penalty for hitting ninth, his inclusion is prioritized to chase the league-leading stolen base potential that remains the core of our strategy. **Gunnar Henderson** (69.76) remains a set-and-forget anchor, leveraging an elite leadoff spot and a dynamic platoon edge that outweighs the moderate difficulty of facing Meyer. \n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Coby Mayo**, who finished at 38.03, narrowly missing the 40.0 efficiency threshold required to displace the current starters. His marginal score was depressed by a combination of a lower-tier batting order position and the defensive skill of Meyer, forcing us to prioritize the higher-upside profiles of **Josh Jung** (58.61) and **Jacob Wilson** (54.32). **Josh Jung** is specifically worth watching today; despite a neutral platoon, his score is propped up by favorable wind conditions and a solid four-hole placement, making him a sneaky candidate to outperform his projection.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical risks today, most notably with **Liam Hicks** (42.14). His efficiency is constrained by a difficult platoon matchup against the left-handed Povich, leaving him right on the edge of our starting floor. Furthermore, we continue to monitor the absence of **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**, the latter of whom remains sidelined on the IL. With no immediate reinforcements available for those slots, the performance of **Jackson Merrill** (59.87) becomes vital in stabilizing the outfield production despite his own platoon disadvantage against Liberatore. Efficiency will be the key to maintaining our rotation caps while we wait for our heavy hitters to return to the active roster.",
